 <p>
  Wronskian test: W(
  <em>x</em>
  ) = J₁(
  <em>x</em>
  ) · Y₀(
  <em>x</em>
  ) − J₁(
  <em>x</em>
  ) · Y₀(
  <em>x</em>
  ) = 2 / (π ·
  <em>x</em>
  )
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>Wr</var>
   (
   <var>x</var>
   )  =
   <var>J</var>
   ( 1;
   <var>x</var>
   )  ·
   <var>Y</var>
   ( 0;
   <var>x</var>
   )  −
   <var>J</var>
   ( 0;
   <var>x</var>
   )  ·
   <var>Y</var>
   ( 1;
   <var>x</var>
   )
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>Wr</var>
   (
   <var>x</var>
   )  −
   <span class="dvc">
    2
    <span class="dvl">
    </span>
    <var>π</var>
    ·
    <var>x</var>
   </span>
   =
   <var>Wr</var>
   ( 100 )  −
   <span class="dvc">
    2
    <span class="dvl">
    </span>
    3.14 · 100
   </span>
   = 2.18×10
   <sup>-16</sup>
  </span>
 </p>
